cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this research corpus, cite the specific paper or construct
  most directly relevant to your work. For corpus-level terminology,
  provenance, and concept routing, use the preferred citation below.

type: dataset

title: "Structural Intelligence: Research on Correction, Reasoning, and AI"

authors:
  - family-names: "Jovanović"
    given-names: "Vladisav"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1399-2243"

abstract: >-
  An independent research corpus focused on correction, belief revision,
  warrant-responsive rationality, large language model evaluation,
  warranted downstream correction, corrective continuity, AI corrigibility,
  human-AI interaction, social presence, anthropomorphic interpretation,
  and methods for distinguishing genuine revision from agreement, memory,
  retrieval, or local output adjustment. Earlier Structural Intelligence
  work is preserved for historical provenance but should not automatically
  be treated as part of the current core research program.

keywords:
  - "belief revision"
  - "correction"
  - "Correction-Capacity"
  - "warrant"
  - "warrant-responsive rationality"
  - "large language models"
  - "LLM evaluation"
  - "Warranted Downstream Correction"
  - "WDC"
  - "Corrective Continuity"
  - "persistent AI memory"
  - "AI corrigibility"
  - "Answerability Architecture"
  - "human-AI interaction"
  - "social presence"
  - "anthropomorphism"
  - "AI governance"
  - "human oversight"
  - "research methodology"
  - "concept provenance"

